meta {
  name: Print All Reports For Order
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/print-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {}
}

tests {
  test("PDF returned", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); expect(res.getHeader("content-type")).to.contain("application/pdf"); });
}

docs {
  Merged PDF of the order's lab reports (optional body: `templateId`, `orderItemIds`).

  Scope: the branch that OWNS the order (orders.branch_id) prints EVERY report on the
  order, whichever branch currently holds it (e.g. tests done at a receiving branch
  after an internal transfer). Every other branch prints only the reports it holds
  itself, exactly as before. An order the caller's branch has nothing to do with gives
  404 ORDER_REPORTS_NOT_FOUND. Pending / partly filled tests print as they are.
  B2B referral-panel ownership is still enforced per report.
  Note: this route has no permission decorator (any authenticated user) - unchanged.

  ## B2B Referral Panel sessions

  A referral panel (B2B) login prints only its own, FINISHED reports. Lab staff are
  not affected: every report on the order is printed, an unfinished one as "Result
  pending".
  - 403 `REFERRAL_PANEL_ACCESS_DENIED` — the order belongs to another panel (or to no
    panel).
  - Unfinished reports (anything other than Approved / Published) are LEFT OUT of the
    document, on both render paths (`lab_all_report` template and the per-report
    merge), and out of "Share and Inform", which prints through this same route.
  - 409 `LAB_REPORT_PRINT_NOT_APPROVED_FOR_PANEL` — none of the order's (or the
    selected `orderItemIds`') reports is Approved or Published yet. Lab staff get
    the usual 404 `ORDER_REPORTS_NOT_FOUND` for an order with no reports instead.
}
